  "sourceTextExcerpts": [
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:3",
      "text": "This man went up out of his city from year to year to worship and to sacrifice to the LORD of Armies in Shiloh. The two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, priests to the LORD, were there.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V3"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:5",
      "text": "but he gave a double portion to Hannah, for he loved Hannah, but the LORD had shut up her womb.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V5"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:6",
      "text": "Her rival provoked her severely, to irritate her, because the LORD had shut up her womb.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V6"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:7",
      "text": "So year by year, when she went up to the LORD’s house, her rival provoked her. Therefore she wept, and didn’t eat.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V7"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:9",
      "text": "So Hannah rose up after they had finished eating and drinking in Shiloh. Now Eli the priest was sitting on his seat by the doorpost of the LORD’s temple.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V9"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:10",
      "text": "She was in bitterness of soul, and prayed to the LORD, weeping bitterly.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V10"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:11",
      "text": "She vowed a vow, and said, “LORD of Armies, if you will indeed look at the affliction of your servant and remember me, and not forget your servant, but will give to your servant a boy, then I will give him to the LORD all the days of his life, and no razor shall come on his head.”",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V11"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:12",
      "text": "As she continued praying before the LORD, Eli saw her mouth.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V12"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 2:32",
      "text": "You will see the affliction of my habitation, in all the wealth which I will give Israel. There shall not be an old man in your house forever.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA02.htm#V32"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 20:2",
      "text": "He said to him, “Far from it; you will not die. Behold, my father does nothing either great or small, but that he discloses it to me. Why would my father hide this thing from me? It is not so.”",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA20.htm#V2"
    }
  ],
